{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game mechanic game mechanic","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","fileName":"Game Mechanic.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Mechanic","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Token","Game Rule","Core Gameplay Loop","Game Genre","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game mechanic game mechanic","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","fileName":"Game Mechanic.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Mechanic","heading":"Game Mechanic","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game mechanic is an identifiable interactive loop formed from [[Game Token|tokens]], [[Game Rule|rules]], the player, and the game. It may be brief, such as drawing a card, or contain many subsystems and take much longer, such as building an empire.\n\nMechanics can recur across otherwise different games because their loop structure is separable from a particular theme. Repeated central mechanics become [[Core Gameplay Loop|core gameplay]] and often help define a [[Game Genre]].\n\nA mechanic becomes legible through a vocabulary of [[Game Verb|player verbs]], objects, and their relationships. Its quality depends less on the number of available actions than on how strongly those actions create choices and reinforce one another.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Token","Game Rule","Core Gameplay Loop","Game Genre","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game mechanic game mechanic","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Mechanic.md","fileName":"Game Mechanic.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Mechanic","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Token","Game Rule","Core Gameplay Loop","Game Genre","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}